---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Command from '../components/Command.astro';
import { REPO_URL, RELEASES_URL } from '../site';
---

<Base title="Download" description="Install OpenWren with apt, dnf or as an AppImage." narrow>
  <h1>Download</h1>
  <p>
    OpenWren runs on Linux. Pick the section for your distribution. The apt and dnf repositories also deliver updates
    through your normal system updates.
  </p>
  <p class="muted">
    <a href="#apt">apt</a> · <a href="#dnf">dnf</a> · <a href="#appimage">AppImage</a> ·
    <a href="#source">Build from source</a> · <a href="#uninstall">Uninstall</a>
  </p>

  <h2 id="apt">Debian, Ubuntu and derivatives (apt)</h2>
  <p>1. Add the signing key.</p>
  <Command code="curl -fsSL https://packages.openwren.app/key.gpg | sudo tee /usr/share/keyrings/openwren.gpg > /dev/null" />
  <p>2. Add the repository.</p>
  <Command
    code={'echo "deb [signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/openwren.gpg] https://packages.openwren.app/apt stable main" | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/openwren.list'}
  />
  <p>3. Install.</p>
  <Command code="sudo apt update && sudo apt install openwren" />

  <h2 id="dnf">Fedora (dnf)</h2>
  <p>1. Add the repository.</p>
  <Command code="sudo dnf config-manager addrepo --from-repofile=https://packages.openwren.app/rpm/openwren.repo" />
  <p>2. Install.</p>
  <Command code="sudo dnf install openwren" />

  <h2 id="appimage">AppImage</h2>
  <p>
    For any other distribution, download the AppImage from the
    <a href={RELEASES_URL}>latest release on GitHub</a>, make the file executable and run it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="uninstall">Uninstall</h2>
  <p>Remove the package with your package manager:</p>
  <Command code="sudo apt remove openwren" />
  <Command code="sudo dnf remove openwren" />
  <p>
    Like other Linux apps, this leaves your own data in place, so that a reinstall finds your accounts and mail again.
    To remove everything, quit OpenWren first (tray icon, then Quit) and run these three commands.
  </p>
  <p>1. The downloaded mail, search index, drafts and settings (the encrypted database).</p>
  <Command code="rm -rf ~/.local/share/org.openwren.app" />
  <p>2. The start-at-login entry.</p>
  <Command code="rm -f ~/.config/autostart/openwren.desktop" />
  <p>3. The account passwords and the database key in the system keyring.</p>
  <Command code="secret-tool clear service OpenWren" />
  <p>
    <code>secret-tool</code> is in the package <code>libsecret-tools</code> (Debian, Ubuntu) or
    <code>libsecret</code> (Fedora). Without it, open "Passwords and Keys", search for "OpenWren" and delete the
    entries. Your mail stays on your mail servers; only the copy on this computer is deleted.
  </p>

  <h2 id="key">Signing key</h2>
  <p>
    The apt and dnf repositories are signed with the OpenWren GPG key. Before you trust the key, compare its
    fingerprint with the one below.
  </p>
  <Command code="8991 7136 148C 9676 F3A5  1B21 4B8A FB6E 4238 18E0" />
  <p>To show the fingerprint of the key you downloaded:</p>
  <Command code="gpg --show-keys --with-fingerprint /usr/share/keyrings/openwren.gpg" />
  <p>More about signing is on the <a href="/security/">security page</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="source">Build from source</h2>
  <p>
    The source code and build instructions are in the <a href={REPO_URL}>repository</a>. You need Node.js with pnpm,
    Rust, and Tauri's Linux libraries.
  </p>
</Base>
